{
  "summary": "Overall the UI follows the DESIGN.md spec – components are built on React‑Native‑Paper, design tokens are imported, and Axe reports no accessibility violations. However, the primary add‑receipt flow is broken because the “Receipt” mini‑FAB is not accessible/rendered, and several screens use incorrect copy or lack required UI elements. A few interaction‑state details (focus‑visible outlines, inline spinners, hard‑coded colors) also drift from the token‑only approach. These high‑impact issues must be fixed before the product can be considered polished.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "Mini‑FABs for “Receipt” and “Mileage” are not rendered with an accessible name; the test cannot locate the “Receipt” button, breaking the add‑entry flow.",
      "fix": "Render MiniFAB components inside FABAdd with `accessibilityLabel=\"Add receipt\"` / `\"Add mileage\"`, set `accessible={true}` and `accessibilityRole=\"button\"`. Ensure they appear when the main FAB is pressed, use the MiniFAB wrapper that applies theme colors, and wire their `onPress` to navigate to the entry screens."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Error view displays a generic message and lacks the required copy “Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.” and a Retry button.",
      "fix": "Update the error UI to use the exact copy from DESIGN.md and include a `PrimaryButton` labeled “Retry” that re‑attempts the policy acceptance when pressed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Passphrase modal does not show the rule text “Passphrase must be at least 12 characters.” before the user starts typing, violating the spec.",
      "fix": "Add a `Text` component (styled with `theme.typography.bodyLarge`) above the two passphrase inputs containing the rule text, ensuring it is always visible when the modal opens."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "During export the buttons are disabled but no inline `ActivityIndicator` is shown, and the “Generating export…” copy is missing, diverging from the spec.",
      "fix": "When `exportRunning` is true, set each button’s `loading` prop or embed a small `ActivityIndicator` inside the button, display the label “Generating export…”, and keep the button disabled."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Field‑level validation messages are not rendered using `HelperText type=\"error\"` under each input, so the exact copy from DESIGN.md is not shown to the user.",
      "fix": "After validation fails, render a `HelperText` component directly under the offending `FormField` with the specific error string (e.g., “Enter a value > 0, ≤ 1 000 000 with up to 2 decimals.”)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus‑visible styling (2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline`) is missing on web, so keyboard navigation lacks a visible focus indicator.",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` style (or `style` prop using `outlineWidth: 2`, `outlineColor: theme.colors.outline`) to `PrimaryButton` (and similar components) so that a visible outline appears when the button receives focus."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Numeric inputs (amount, miles, rates) do not enforce `maxLength` matching the allowed digit limits and lack appropriate `autoComplete`/`keyboardType` configuration, leading to overflow and inconsistent UX.",
      "fix": "Add `maxLength` props (e.g., 9 for amount, 5 for miles), set `keyboardType=\"numeric\"`, and include `autoComplete=\"off\"` or a suitable auto‑complete value for each numeric `FormField`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Card title text color is hard‑coded as `#212121` instead of using `theme.colors.onSurface`, breaking token consistency.",
      "fix": "Replace the literal color with `theme.colors.onSurface` (or the appropriate token) via the style prop or by letting Paper’s theme handle it."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Component uses a CSS class name `empty-state` without a matching rule in `public/theme.css`, leaving the element unstyled.",
      "fix": "Either remove the unused class name or add a rule to `public/theme.css` that styles `.empty-state` using the design tokens for spacing, colors, and typography."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Settings error state shows a Snackbar but does not provide a retry action; while not mandatory, the spec’s error view expects a clear retry path.",
      "fix": "Add an optional “Retry” action button to the Snackbar that re‑loads the settings when tapped, or ensure the copy matches the spec exactly."
    }
  ]
}

