{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "The UI flow test fails at step 22 \"click button \\\"Receipt\\\"\" for both phone and desktop sizes, indicating the \"Receipt\" button is not present or not interactable after clicking the Dashboard tab. This likely stems from recent changes that affect the FAB or receipt entry UI, breaking the expected UI flow. Verify and restore the mini FAB \"Receipt\" button (or its accessibility label) so the acceptance flow can locate and click it.",
    "In src/lib/backup.ts, restoreBackup uses FileSystem.readDirectoryAsync and FileSystem.deleteAsync which are now deprecated in the Expo SDK, causing runtime warnings and potentially failing tests that expect the new File API usage. Replace these legacy calls with the new expo-file-system File/Directory classes or import from \"expo-file-system/legacy\" to avoid deprecation errors.",
    "The backup temporary file cleanup after sharing should also delete the temporary file after the share sheet closes (including on failure or cancel). The current implementation in src/lib/files.ts (saveAndShare) already deletes the file after sharing but uses the legacy writeAsStringAsync and deleteAsync. Ensure it uses the new File API for writing and cleaning up temporary files, and update createBackup/restoreBackup to handle cleanup correctly."
  ],
  "feedback": "Fix the missing Receipt button in the UI flow and replace deprecated expo-file-system methods with the new File API in backup and restoration logic. Ensure temporary backup files are deleted after sharing in all scenarios. After these corrections, all acceptance tests and unit tests should pass."
}

