      "file": "src/screens/RestoreScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "After a successful restore the UI never shows the \"Data restored successfully.\" Snackbar, so the primary backup‑restore flow cannot be verified and the user receives no confirmation.",
      "fix": "In the restore flow, after `restoreBackup` resolves, trigger a `Snackbar` (or `Toast`) with `visible=true`, `children='Data restored successfully.'` and an appropriate `accessibilityLiveRegion='assertive'`. Ensure the Snackbar is rendered at a top level (e.g., via a context or portal) so it appears even if the screen is unmounted."
