{
  "summary": "The UI implements the core flow defined in DESIGN.md and clears automated accessibility (axe) and Lighthouse checks. All primary screens (policy gate, dashboard, receipt & mileage lists, entry forms, settings, export, backup/restore, and delete‑all confirmation) load and navigate correctly on both phone and desktop. However, several secondary states, copy details, and a few accessibility nuances are missing or inconsistent with the spec. These issues are mostly medium‑severity and can be fixed without breaking the primary user journey.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/PolicyScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The error state required by the spec (full‑screen error view with the message “Unable to store your acceptance. Please try again.” and a **Retry** button) is not implemented; only loading and default states exist.",
      "fix": "Add an error UI branch that renders a full‑screen view with the exact copy and a Retry button that re‑executes the acceptance storage logic."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/HomeScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Dashboard error view is missing the copy “Pull down to retry.” – the Retry UI exists but the message does not match the spec, potentially confusing users.",
      "fix": "Update the error component to include the exact copy string and ensure pull‑to‑refresh triggers a retry."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "EmptyState component shows the title and primary button but omits the description text “Tap the + button to add your first receipt.” required by the design.",
      "fix": "Pass the description prop to `EmptyState` so the full copy appears under the title."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/ReceiptsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "EmptyState uses hard‑coded color values for text/background instead of the design tokens (e.g., `#212121` instead of `theme.colors.onSurface`).",
      "fix": "Replace raw color literals with values from `theme.colors` via the Paper theme or CSS custom properties."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/MileageScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "EmptyState title reads “No mileage recorded” while the spec specifies “No mileage logged”.",
      "fix": "Change the title string to match the exact spec copy."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/BackupPassphraseScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The rule text “Passphrase must be at least 12 characters.” that should appear above the passphrase inputs is not rendered; only live validation messages are shown.",
      "fix": "Add a static `Text` element above the inputs containing the rule copy, styled with the body text token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/RestoreScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The passphrase entry for restore uses only a placeholder and lacks an associated visible `label`, violating both the spec and accessibility requirements.",
      "fix": "Add a `FormField` with a `label=\"Backup passphrase\"` prop; keep the placeholder for guidance but ensure the label is linked via `accessibilityLabel`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Offline banner defined in DESIGN.md (full‑screen message “You are offline…”) is not displayed on any screen that may trigger a network request (e.g., ExportScreen).",
      "fix": "Create an `OfflineBanner` component that conditionally renders based on NetInfo state and include it in screens where a network call could occur."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FABAdd.tsx",
      "issue": "MiniFABs (receipt & mileage) lack a visible focus‑outline on web; keyboard users cannot see when a FAB has focus.",
      "fix": "Add a focus‑visible style (2 dp outline using `theme.colors.outline`) to the MiniFABs and ensure `onFocus`/`onBlur` toggle the outline."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/screens/DeleteAllDataScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Delete‑all‑data confirmation dialog does not trap focus; users can tab out of the modal while it is open, which breaks modal accessibility patterns.",
      "fix": "Wrap dialog content with a focus‑trap component (e.g., `react-native-focus-trap` or manage focus manually) so that tabbing cycles within the dialog."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Numeric fields (amount, miles, rates) lack a `maxLength` prop and do not truncate input beyond the allowed maximum, contrary to the “Edge – very long numbers” requirement.",
      "fix": "Add `maxLength` derived from the validation limits (e.g., 7 digits for amount) and ensure overflow triggers the same validation error helper text."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "src/screens/SettingsScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The screen does not include explicit ARIA landmarks (`role=\"navigation\"` for the settings list, `role=\"main\"` for content).",
      "fix": "Add appropriate `accessibilityRole` / `role` props to the container elements to provide clear landmarks for assistive technologies."
    }
  ]
}

